
Proportional colocalization test
-----------------------------------
          Method  eta p_coloc
 prop-coloc-cond 0.11    TRUE
 prop-coloc-full 0.10    0.06
-----------------------------------

p_coloc assesses proportional colocalization hypothesis (rejection indicates failure to colocalize).
Proportional colocalization is suggested when the proportional colocalization hypothesis is not rejected.
p_coloc = TRUE indicates proportional colocalization hypothesis is rejected at an alpha = 0.05 significance level.
Proportional colocalization test
-----------------------------------
          Method  eta p_coloc
 prop-coloc-cond   NA      NA
 prop-coloc-full 0.00    0.00
-----------------------------------

p_coloc assesses proportional colocalization hypothesis (rejection indicates failure to colocalize).
Proportional colocalization is suggested when the proportional colocalization hypothesis is not rejected.
A model of proportional colocalization based on lead variants is rejected. 
Therefore, prop-coloc-cond rejects the null hypothesis of proportional colocalization.
Proportional colocalization test
-----------------------------------
          Method  eta p_coloc
 prop-coloc-cond 0.13   FALSE
 prop-coloc-full 0.37    0.00
-----------------------------------

p_coloc assesses proportional colocalization hypothesis (rejection indicates failure to colocalize).
Proportional colocalization is suggested when the proportional colocalization hypothesis is not rejected.
p_coloc = FALSE indicates proportional colocalization hypothesis is not rejected at an alpha = 0.05 significance level.